// Public-release proof guard: hold publication while a release note bound for
// a public surface has no required proof behind it. PUBLIC_CANDIDATE is 1 when
// the candidate is going somewhere outside the organisation;
// REQUIRED_PROOF_AVAILABLE is 1 once every claim the host requires evidence
// for - a green run, a signed artifact, a linked receipt - is actually
// retrievable.
// PUBLIC_RELEASE_NOT_PROVEN is a disjunction: either the proof is missing or
// the copy was never validated. Baseline Nano IR carries an and-chain and has
// no `or` node, so the two halves are two entries, the way event_volatility
// splits a bull and a bear term rather than signing one series. This file is
// the proof half; aether_release_notes_copy_unvalidated is the copy half. Both
// map to the same reason code, and a host deploying one without the other has
// deployed half a guard.
// This rule gates release-note publication and nothing else. It must never be
// wired to a branch, a deploy, or an engineering merge: unproven copy is a
// reason not to publish a claim, never a reason to block engineering work.
// REGIME: all of them, for public surfaces only. An internal candidate has
// PUBLIC_CANDIDATE 0 and this rule is silent on it by construction.
// CONDITIONS: the host decides what counts as required proof for a given
// surface before publishing the boolean, and publishes 0 when it does not know
// rather than assuming the proof exists.
// INVALIDATION: the proof becoming retrievable. The rule proposes a hold; it
// does not latch and does not decide when the hold ends.
// SHAPE: 5m, matching the rest of the release-note family so one batch is
// evaluated by every rule on the same tick.
// NOT aether_release_notes_copy_unvalidated: that is the other half of the
// same disjunction and asks whether the words were checked. This one asks
// whether the evidence behind the words can be fetched at all.
// CALIBRATED ON: nothing numeric; both comparisons are against host booleans.
// What does not travel is the proof policy - which claims need evidence on
// which surface is the publishing organisation's decision.
strategy AetherReleaseNotesProofMissing {

    agent ReleaseDesk

    every 5m {

        if PUBLIC_CANDIDATE >= 1 and REQUIRED_PROOF_AVAILABLE <= 0 {

            pause()

        }

    }

}
